| [blender/agent-harness](https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything/tree/main/blender/agent-harness "This path skips through empty directories") | [blender/agent-harness](https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything/tree/main/blender/agent-harness "This path skips through empty directories") | [Fix Windows path escape in generated Blender render script (](https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything/commit/b7451aff88249f2d8ccfc209c0adfa399dd6150e "Fix Windows path escape in generated Blender render script (#390)  Use repr() (via f-string !r) for path embedding instead of raw-string r'...' prefixes. Raw strings are fragile with trailing backslashes and quotes in paths; repr() produces a correctly-escaped Python literal for any path.  Affects three sites in bpy_gen.py: - HDRI image path in _gen_world_settings - Output filepath in _gen_render_output - 'Render complete:' print statement in _gen_render_output  Fixes #343") [#390](https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything/pull/390) [)](https://github.com/HKUDS/CLI-Anything/commit/b7451aff88249f2d8ccfc209c0adfa399dd6150e "Fix Windows path escape in generated Blender render script (#390)  Use repr() (via f-string !r) for path embedding instead of raw-string r'...' prefixes. Raw strings are fragile with trailing backslashes and quotes in paths; repr() produces a correctly-escaped Python literal for any path.  Affects three sites in bpy_gen.py: - HDRI image path in _gen_world_settings - Output filepath in _gen_render_output - 'Render complete:' print statement in _gen_render_output  Fixes #343") | 2 months agoAug 3, 2026 |
